 ## Overview
-Volume Feature Rendering (VFR) is a differentiable rendering technique that integrates queried feature vectors along a ray into a single aggregated feature vector, which is then transformed into the final pixel color by a single neural network evaluation [S1][S2][S3, unofficial]. Unlike standard volume rendering, which requires $N$ neural network evaluations (one per sample) to predict color, VFR reduces the number of evaluations to one, thereby relieving the framework from the high computational cost associated with large color networks [S1][S2][S3, unofficial]. This allows for the use of significantly larger neural networks to improve rendering quality without increasing training or rendering time proportionally [S1][S2][S3, unofficial].
