 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Training time is significantly reduced compared to standard volume rendering with large networks. For example, VFR achieves state-of-the-art quality in 2.9–3.3 minutes (20K steps) on the NeRF synthetic dataset, compared to Zip-NeRF's 7.7 hours on a V100 GPU [S1][S2][S3, unofficial]. The rendering time is 4–5 frames per second at 800x800 resolution on the NeRF synthetic dataset, and 1–2 frames per second at 1300x840 on the real-world 360 dataset [S1][S2][S3, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Not explicitly given, but the reduction in NN evaluations reduces the memory footprint associated with storing intermediate NN states during backpropagation compared to reverse-mode AD [S5].
